<title>UK: Cazenove Indian GDR Index down 1.14 percent.</title>
<headline>Cazenove Indian GDR Index down 1.14 percent.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Cazenove Indian GDR Index fell 0.79 points, 1.14 percent, to 68.46 points after the Bombay Stock Exchange 30 share index shed 66.96 points to 3,172.98.</p>
<p>The premium for GDRs over stocks on the local market was 7.34 percent.</p>
<p>The Cazenove index is a capitalisation weighted basket of Indian global depositary receipts and measures the change from midday on the previous trading day to midday today.</p>
<p>-- David Chance, London newsroom +44 171 542 5887</p>
